'''thorogummite''' (thō-rō-gum′īt), ''n.'' [< ''thorium'' + ''gummite.''] A mineral occurring in massive forms of a dull yellowish-brown color, and containing silica and the oxids of uranium, thorium, and the metals of the cerium and yttrium groups.
{{smaller block|It is somewhat related to gummite, but is distinguished by containing thorium. It occurs with gadolinite and other rare minerals in Llano county, Texas.}}

